  "query_preview": "..Main weather story continues to be warm and dry \nconditions with typical afternoon breeziness each afternoon thru the \nupcoming weekend. The main source of the breeziness is a series of \nimpulses embedded within a broader relatively dry westerly to \nsouthwesterly flow aloft. I anticipate these embedded shortwave \ndisturbances tomorrow into Thursday and again on Saturday into \nSunday to enhance breezy conditions across southeast Arizona. \nImpacts we could see from these impulses include elevated fire \nweather concerns, hazy skies, and the familiar struggle of keeping \nthose lighter patio furniture items and garbage cans in an upright \nposition.\n\nTomorrow, Thursday, and especially Saturday are looking to be the \nwindiest days of the forecast period with west to southwest winds of \n15 to 20 mph and accompanying periodic gusts to around 30 mph. \nCompared to most recent windy days we've seen, winds will peak in \nthe mid afternoon hours coinciding with the driest part of the day \nrather than in the morning. Minimum RH will be in the 10% to 20% \nrange, although a subtle moisture increase will begin to nudge in \nfrom west to east on Saturday. Overall, there is a 20 to 40 percent \nchance for elevated fire weather conditions tomorrow thru Friday \neast of Tucson increasing to 30 to 50 percent on Saturday.",
